# ===== Environment & secrets =====
# Never commit any .env file with real values. Only .env.example is tracked.
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
# Timestamped backups written by scripts/set-master-key.mjs. These hold the SAME
# real credentials as .env.local, and the bare ".env.local" pattern above does NOT
# match them -- one `git add .` away from committing live secrets.
.env*.bak-*
.env*.local

# ===== Database backups =====
# Written by production/scripts/backup-db.mjs before every migration. Measured on the
# 25 Aug 2026 backup: 117 tables, 1,793 rows, and 25 of those tables carry personal
# data -- 64 contacts with addresses, emails and phones; 29 leads with GSTINs; 25
# customers; 93 inbound emails.
#
# And one column is worse than personal data: `quotes.public_token`. That is the
# capability token in a quote's public accept URL, so a committed backup is a list of
# links anybody can open without logging in. The file also names the prod project ref.
#
# The script takes its output directory as an argument, so BOTH patterns are here --
# the directory used today, and the filename wherever somebody points it next.
backups/
**/backups/
resellersos-data-*.json

